      "id": "A01",
      "label": "percentage price at an exact half cent: 0.25 * 50 % = 0.125 rounds half away from zero to 0.13 (banker's rounding and truncation give 0.12)",
      "traps": [
        "numeric-rounding"
      ],
      "reasoning": "T-SQL ROUND(@UnitPrice * @HighestDiscountPercentage / 100.0, 2) rounds an exact midpoint away from zero. 0.25 * 50.000 / 100.0 is exactly 0.125, and the digit before the 5 is even, so round-half-to-even gives 0.12, truncation gives 0.12, and only half-away-from-zero gives 0.13. The hand-derived case (2.49875) is not a midpoint, so it separates rounding from truncation but not from banker's rounding.",
      "fixedCase": {
